{
  "area": "props-containers",
  "description": "Container rules (Features WV2, P6.core; CROSS-ENGINE-FEATURES §4, 6. Inventory, shop, props, interiors; catalog items-containers): whether a chest, barrel or crate can be opened, unlocked, taken from or put into, whether it is due to respawn, and which are at a place. The moves themselves are the trade model's (ui/trade-cases.json); this is the gate in front of them. Ops: view {container, context?} -> {view}; unlock {container, context?} -> {result, container}; move {container, move: {kind: take} | {kind: put, itemId}, context?} -> {refusal}; at {containers, location} -> {ids}; respawn {container, now} -> {due}. context is {playerItemIds?, buildings?: [{id, interior: bool}], now?}. Every case is {name, op, input, expected}; numbers compare within tolerance, everything else exactly, object key sets included (a key TypeScript leaves undefined is absent). Runner: src/props/props-corpus.ts. Regenerate with npm run props-corpora; npm run props-corpora:check fails on any difference.",
  "version": 1,
  "tolerance": 1e-9,
  "sources": [
    "core game-engine/logic/ContainerManager.ts (toState defaults, isFull, canUnlock, unlock, shouldRespawn, getContainersAtLocation), now delegating shouldRespawn to src/props/containers.ts.",
    "core ContainerIR (ir-types.ts): buildingId, location interior | outdoor.",
    "pipelines origin/main 9b6a897: pipelines/game-export/ir-generator.ts generateContainerPlacements (every container location interior, its position a world-frame point inside the building's footprint); Godot merge finding M2-4 (219 Aldermoor containers inside solid houses).",
    "pipelines origin/main 5328ed2: pipelines/generators/interior-generator.ts states an interior only on the building a content-keyed rule picks (a settlement's eating house, when any exported text is found at a cafe or restaurant: a Restaurant, Cafe, Tavern or Inn for a text at a cafe or restaurant, and since pipelines origin/main 55985db a Bar for a text at a cafe only, preferred last) and interior: null on every other, so every other building's interior containers stay unreachable (no_interior)."
  ],
  "contract": {
    "defaultCapacity": 10,
    "states": [
      "open",
      "locked",
      "unreachable"
    ],
    "refusals": [
      "unknown_building",
      "no_interior",
      "locked",
      "full"
    ],
    "unlockResults": [
      "unlocked",
      "not_locked",
      "no_key_item",
      "key_missing"
    ],
    "normalise": "capacity 10 unless a finite number is stated; items [] unless an array; locked and respawns false unless stated (ContainerManager.toState)",
    "reach": "a container at location interior is reachable only when its buildingId names a listed building that states an interior; unlisted -> unknown_building, no interior -> no_interior; outdoor or no location is always reachable. Interiors are stated by pipelines/atelier, never invented",
    "order": "unknown_building / no_interior, then locked, then (a put) full",
    "capacity": "slots, not quantities: full when items.length >= capacity; slotsFree = max(0, capacity - items.length); a put that stacks onto an entry with the same itemId is allowed when full",
    "unlock": "unreachable -> its refusal; not locked -> not_locked; no keyItemId -> no_key_item; key not held -> key_missing; else unlocked and the record comes back with locked false. Lock picking is P9b",
    "respawn": "due when respawns, lastOpenedAt and now are valid times, respawnTimeMinutes > 0 and (now - lastOpenedAt) / 60000 >= respawnTimeMinutes; now is an ISO date-time or epoch milliseconds the host passes",
    "at": "ids in input order of containers whose businessId, residenceId or lotId equals a non-empty one of the location"
  },
  "cases": [
    {
